01:08:31,000 --> 01:08:35,000
And you've shown your experiments with all of the configurations that would-

1161
01:08:35,000 --> 01:08:36,000
Not all of them.

1162
01:08:36,000 --> 01:08:37,000
Okay.

1163
01:08:37,000 --> 01:08:39,000
We have to keep some stuff quiet.

1164
01:08:39,000 --> 01:08:40,000
Okay.

1165
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:41,000
Cool.

1166
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:47,000
So are you doing like lateral propeller experiments or are you doing things that involve like

1167
01:08:47,000 --> 01:08:48,000
lifting objects?

1168
01:08:48,000 --> 01:08:51,000
We're not lifting objects yet in Earth's gravity.

1169
01:08:51,000 --> 01:08:52,000
Okay.

1170
01:08:52,000 --> 01:08:54,000
We're measuring the forces of these objects.

1171
01:08:54,000 --> 01:08:55,000
Yeah.

1172
01:08:55,000 --> 01:09:00,000
And seeing how much their force can lift as compared to Earth's gravity.

1173
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:01,000
Got it.

1174
01:09:01,000 --> 01:09:05,000
So we do have thrusters that are theoretically capable to lift themselves up.

1175
01:09:05,000 --> 01:09:10,030
The problem is all of the hardware that goes with it, the voltages and the powers and

1176
01:09:10,030 --> 01:09:13,030
the wires and the framing and all that other stuff is not there yet.

1177
01:09:13,030 --> 01:09:19,350
So you'd have to, it's like saying your car engine can lift the engine, can move the engine

1178
01:09:19,350 --> 01:09:23,350
down the street, but no tires and no frames and it's not very useful.

1179
01:09:23,350 --> 01:09:24,350
Sure.

1180
01:09:24,350 --> 01:09:28,350
But for right now, for what we have for lunar applications, space applications, it's awesome.

1181
01:09:28,350 --> 01:09:30,350
It would be fantastic.

1182
01:09:30,350 --> 01:09:31,350
That's amazing.

1183
01:09:31,350 --> 01:09:36,350
So in microgravity or no gravity environments, you'll get a ton of thrust.

1184
01:09:36,350 --> 01:09:37,350
Sure.

1185
01:09:37,350 --> 01:09:38,350
That's amazing.

1186
01:09:38,350 --> 01:09:41,350
And you're seeing weight reduction, is that right?

1187
01:09:41,350 --> 01:09:45,350
Well, we were saying that, yeah, the weight reduction would be something we're seeing,

1188
01:09:45,350 --> 01:09:46,350
not mass reduction.

1189
01:09:46,350 --> 01:09:47,350
Be careful.

1190
01:09:47,350 --> 01:09:48,350
Okay.

1191
01:09:48,350 --> 01:09:49,350
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1192
01:09:49,350 --> 01:09:51,350
No, I know that gets thrown around in the UFO world all the time.

1193
01:09:51,350 --> 01:09:54,350
You're like, wait, are you reducing the mass of the thing?

1194
01:09:54,350 --> 01:09:56,350
It's definitely not negative mass.

1195
01:09:56,350 --> 01:09:57,350
Yeah, yeah, yeah, right.

1196
01:09:57,350 --> 01:09:59,350
But yes, we do those tests.

1197
01:09:59,350 --> 01:10:00,350
We have videos.

1198
01:10:00,350 --> 01:10:01,350
I can share some with you.

1199
01:10:01,350 --> 01:10:02,350
Please.

1200
01:10:02,350 --> 01:10:06,350
Where we put stuff on a scale and we turn it on, it gets lighter, you flip it over, it

1201
01:10:06,350 --> 01:10:07,350
gets heavier.

1202
01:10:07,350 --> 01:10:08,350
We are going through a peer review.

1203
01:10:08,350 --> 01:10:09,350
Okay, amazing.

1204
01:10:09,350 --> 01:10:10,350
For our second pad.

1205
01:10:10,350 --> 01:10:11,350
Oh, cool.

1206
01:10:11,350 --> 01:10:14,350
So the examiner's office is doing a thorough peer review.

1207
01:10:14,350 --> 01:10:17,350
They're the ones going down that path.

1208
01:10:17,350 --> 01:10:18,350
Okay, great.

1209
01:10:18,350 --> 01:10:21,350
Which is apparently equivalent to a scientific peer review.

1210
01:10:21,350 --> 01:10:23,350
So that's what I've been told.

1211
01:10:23,350 --> 01:10:24,350
Amazing.

1212
01:10:24,350 --> 01:10:27,350
So they're reaching out to the people that have done it, reaching out to people who have

1213
01:10:27,350 --> 01:10:30,350
signed affidavits to say, yes, I've seen it, yes, I've reproduced it, blah, blah, blah,

1214
01:10:30,350 --> 01:10:31,350
blah, blah.

1215
01:10:31,350 --> 01:10:32,350
So they're going through that process now.

1216
01:10:32,350 --> 01:10:36,350
What inspired you to pursue kind of more exotic propulsion to begin with?

1217
01:10:36,350 --> 01:10:40,350
Did you have any childhood experiences around this sort of stuff?

1218
01:10:40,350 --> 01:10:41,350
Yes.

1219
01:10:41,350 --> 01:10:42,350
Yes, I did.

1220
01:10:42,350 --> 01:10:50,350
I've always had a fascination with UFOs and I think it's been around a long time.

1221
01:10:50,350 --> 01:10:53,350
Just strange phenomena, but I think it really hit home.

1222
01:10:53,350 --> 01:10:57,350
I think I was 11 or 12 when we worked our haunted house.

1223
01:10:57,350 --> 01:11:01,350
My dad would make haunted houses in our garage in New York.

1224
01:11:01,350 --> 01:11:02,350
Really?

1225
01:11:02,350 --> 01:11:03,350
What does that even mean?

1226
01:11:03,350 --> 01:11:05,350
Make haunted houses in your garage?

1227
01:11:05,350 --> 01:11:10,700
He built a haunted house for the hotel that he worked at.

1228
01:11:10,700 --> 01:11:14,700
A giant Holiday Inn, I think it was, or Hilton in Connecticut.

1229
01:11:14,700 --> 01:11:16,700
And it was a massive haunted house.

1230
01:11:16,700 --> 01:11:18,700
And his job was to build the whole darn thing.

1231
01:11:18,700 --> 01:11:19,700
So he liked that.

1232
01:11:19,700 --> 01:11:21,700
So the next year we did it at our house.

1233
01:11:21,700 --> 01:11:25,700
And we charged people like 50 cents to get in and go through the haunted house.

1234
01:11:25,700 --> 01:11:31,920
And it was probably, I think it was a 9 by 11 single car garage haunted house.

1235
01:11:31,920 --> 01:11:34,020
And we made $1,100.

1236
01:11:34,020 --> 01:11:35,020
That's how many people showed up.

1237
01:11:35,020 --> 01:11:36,020
It was crazy.

1238
01:11:36,020 --> 01:11:39,020
It was a lot of fun.

1239
01:11:39,020 --> 01:11:43,400
But we had a haunted house and it would go on for several weeks.

1240
01:11:43,400 --> 01:11:49,850
One night while I was there working it, a whole bunch of cars came into the driveway.

1241
01:11:49,850 --> 01:11:51,850
And I recognized one of the kids getting out of the car.

1242
01:11:51,850 --> 01:11:53,850
He said, Charlie, go look at that.

1243
01:11:53,850 --> 01:11:58,850
And he shows me, we look up and there's these six bright white lights at the top of the trees,

1244
01:11:58,850 --> 01:12:03,850
just hanging over the trees, just going over the road, just not moving very fast.

1245
01:12:03,850 --> 01:12:05,850
Just hanging out in formation.

1246
01:12:05,850 --> 01:12:07,850
No sound, no wind, no nothing.

1247
01:12:07,850 --> 01:12:11,850
And all these cars were following these lights for several days.

1248
01:12:11,850 --> 01:12:13,850
This happened over a course of several days.

1249
01:12:13,850 --> 01:12:17,850
Was this like a famous UFO wave or flap or something?

1250
01:12:17,850 --> 01:12:19,850
It was. It was in the papers and all that jazz.

1251
01:12:19,850 --> 01:12:21,850
Southeast New York in the mid-80s.

1252
01:12:21,850 --> 01:12:23,850
It was a lot of fun.

1253
01:12:23,850 --> 01:12:26,850
You know, I thought that was pretty cool.

1254
01:12:26,850 --> 01:12:31,850
So I kind of like geared my career towards trying to understand some of that stuff.

1255
01:12:31,850 --> 01:12:33,850
I just wanted to know what the heck that was.

1256
01:12:33,850 --> 01:12:37,880
And it got me interested in physics, I think, and science in general.

1257
01:12:37,880 --> 01:12:39,880
I was always interested in science.

1258
01:12:39,880 --> 01:12:43,880
Did they look like orbs or were they part of a formation?

1259
01:12:43,880 --> 01:12:45,880
Or do you think they were part of the same craft?

1260
01:12:45,880 --> 01:12:46,880
I think they were different craft.

1261
01:12:46,880 --> 01:12:49,880
I think they were just separate crafts.

1262
01:12:49,880 --> 01:12:51,880
I didn't see a solid object or anything.

1263
01:12:51,880 --> 01:12:53,880
And so this was for days at a time.

1264
01:12:53,880 --> 01:12:54,880
They would come every night.

1265
01:12:54,880 --> 01:12:57,880
They'd come back and they'd be in different parts of the city.

1266
01:12:57,880 --> 01:13:00,880
I don't know what the heck they were doing or why they were there.

1267
01:13:00,880 --> 01:13:03,880
But it was pretty cool, pretty wild.

1268
01:13:03,880 --> 01:13:10,200
This is about the same time where somebody said they saw the men in black,

1269
01:13:10,200 --> 01:13:12,200
which I thought was hysterical.

1270
01:13:12,200 --> 01:13:13,200
Wild.

1271
01:13:13,200 --> 01:13:15,200
Because we were trick-or-treating out with my friends.

1272
01:13:15,200 --> 01:13:17,200
And we ran into another group of friends.

1273
01:13:17,200 --> 01:13:22,200
And that group of friends said, hey, these two weird guys showed up in these 1920s outfits.

1274
01:13:22,200 --> 01:13:30,200
And they said, if you see something weird, they said, just close your eyes and tell it to land.

1275
01:13:30,200 --> 01:13:32,200
Do you guys know what the heck that means?

1276
01:13:32,200 --> 01:13:34,200
I knew what it was.

1277
01:13:34,200 --> 01:13:35,200
I said, where are these guys?

1278
01:13:35,200 --> 01:13:36,200
They're right over there.

1279
01:13:36,200 --> 01:13:39,200
So we went running to go look for them, but I didn't find anybody.

1280
01:13:39,200 --> 01:13:41,200
But you knew of the men in black?

1281
01:13:41,200 --> 01:13:42,200
I knew the phenomena.

1282
01:13:42,200 --> 01:13:45,200
No one knew what the men in black were in the 1980s, early 80s.

1283
01:13:45,200 --> 01:13:48,200
I don't think that was a thing, but I'd like to study that stuff.

1284
01:13:48,200 --> 01:13:50,200
So I knew with who that was or what that was.

1285
01:13:50,200 --> 01:13:51,200
That's fascinating.

1286
01:13:51,200 --> 01:13:53,200
So I thought, oh, this is cool.

1287
01:13:53,200 --> 01:13:55,200
How can we learn more about this UFO flap?

1288
01:13:56,200 --> 01:14:01,200
Does it have kind of a name that it's been kind of preserved by, or is there a way to search it?

1289
01:14:01,200 --> 01:14:03,200
You could just look up Brewster, New York.

1290
01:14:03,200 --> 01:14:04,200
Brewster, New York.

1291
01:14:04,200 --> 01:14:05,200
OK.

1292
01:14:05,200 --> 01:14:07,200
Probably 86 or 85, somewhere in that range.

1293
01:14:07,200 --> 01:14:08,200
Wild.

1294
01:14:08,200 --> 01:14:13,200
Newspapers and television almost weekly carried reports of the sightings.

1295
01:14:13,200 --> 01:14:20,900
From different places throughout the area, eyewitnesses all reported seeing the same thing.

1296
01:14:20,900 --> 01:14:24,090
I looked up and right over my head, virtually.

1297
01:14:24,090 --> 01:14:25,090
It wasn't far off.

1298
01:14:25,090 --> 01:14:27,090
It was right over my head and very still.

1299
01:14:27,090 --> 01:14:30,090
It was a room of lights in the shape of a triangle.

1300
01:14:30,090 --> 01:14:32,090
It was just a tremendous object.

1301
01:14:32,090 --> 01:14:37,090
It was anywhere from wingtip to wingtip, about 50 or 60 yards.

1302
01:14:37,090 --> 01:14:40,090
These were very, very unusual lights.

1303
01:14:40,090 --> 01:14:42,090
I've never seen anything like it in my life.

1304
01:14:42,090 --> 01:14:45,090
And so I pulled my car over and I had to take a look.

1305
01:14:45,090 --> 01:14:47,090
But it was in the paper.

1306
01:14:47,090 --> 01:14:49,090
I remember that because it lasted several days.

1307
01:14:49,090 --> 01:14:53,090
And you hinted to me that you had an even more surreal experience.

1308
01:14:53,090 --> 01:14:55,090
That was not a surreal experience.

1309
01:14:55,090 --> 01:14:57,090
That was just me seeing some lights.

1310
01:14:57,090 --> 01:14:59,090
Surreal for many people.

1311
01:14:59,090 --> 01:15:00,090
Just lights.

1312
01:15:00,090 --> 01:15:01,090
It was lights.

1313
01:15:01,090 --> 01:15:08,920
But I had a more intense experience, I would say, many years later.

1314
01:15:08,920 --> 01:15:11,920
My wife and I experienced this.

1315
01:15:11,920 --> 01:15:16,920
And this was a pretty cool event now that it's over.

1316
01:15:16,920 --> 01:15:18,920
A little terrifying at the time.

1317
01:15:18,920 --> 01:15:20,920
But we live in Cocoa Beach.

1318
01:15:20,920 --> 01:15:22,920
So we went out to the beach one night.

1319
01:15:22,920 --> 01:15:24,920
I would say 9.30, 10 o'clock at night.

1320
01:15:24,920 --> 01:15:28,310
And the only ones there.

1321
01:15:28,310 --> 01:15:30,310
It's not uncommon, though, back then.

1322
01:15:30,310 --> 01:15:32,660
This was maybe 10 years ago.

1323
01:15:32,660 --> 01:15:35,490
And maybe 12 years ago.

1324
01:15:35,490 --> 01:15:40,620
So we live close to the Patrick Air Force Base, which is south of us.

1325
01:15:40,620 --> 01:15:46,620
And so out in the ocean, maybe about three miles outside, south of us in the ocean.

1326
01:15:46,620 --> 01:15:47,620
I would say about three miles.

1327
01:15:47,620 --> 01:15:51,620
You kind of gauge how far things are apart because we're used to all the rivers,

1328
01:15:51,620 --> 01:15:52,620
and they're all three miles wide.

1329
01:15:52,620 --> 01:15:54,620
So this is about three miles out in the ocean.

1330
01:15:54,620 --> 01:15:55,620
We see a red light.

1331
01:15:55,620 --> 01:15:56,840
Just a beacon.

1332
01:15:56,840 --> 01:15:57,840
Just bleeping.

1333
01:15:57,840 --> 01:15:59,160
No big deal.

1334
01:15:59,160 --> 01:16:02,160
Just a boat.

1335
01:16:02,160 --> 01:16:03,160
Thousands of boats.

1336
01:16:03,160 --> 01:16:04,160
But not that night.

1337
01:16:04,160 --> 01:16:06,360
Or not thousands of boats.

1338
01:16:06,360 --> 01:16:08,360
And it gets brighter.

1339
01:16:08,360 --> 01:16:09,360
And it gets brighter.

1340
01:16:09,360 --> 01:16:12,520
We're like, man, that's getting kind of bright.

1341
01:16:12,520 --> 01:16:13,520
What is that?

1342
01:16:13,520 --> 01:16:16,680
You know, beacons don't get that bright.

1343
01:16:16,680 --> 01:16:17,680
So it's got to be a boat.

1344
01:16:17,680 --> 01:16:20,280
Maybe someone's in trouble.

1345
01:16:20,280 --> 01:16:21,280
And then it gets really bright.

1346
01:16:21,280 --> 01:16:23,670
And then it explodes.

1347
01:16:23,670 --> 01:16:29,370
So we see this giant, I don't want to say mushroom cloud, but it got very, very bright.

1348
01:16:29,370 --> 01:16:33,110
So bright it lit up the whole beach as far as the eye can see.

1349
01:16:33,110 --> 01:16:36,110
You know, all the way from Cape Canaveral, all the way down.

1350
01:16:36,110 --> 01:16:39,430
And I said, my God, what the heck happened there?

1351
01:16:39,430 --> 01:16:41,430
My wife and I were like, that's crazy.

1352
01:16:41,430 --> 01:16:45,560
Clearly someone's going to call the police and tell them that a boat exploded.

1353
01:16:45,560 --> 01:16:46,560
You know, we're on the beach.

1354
01:16:46,560 --> 01:16:48,560
We didn't have phones or anything at the time.

1355
01:16:48,560 --> 01:16:52,280
Like, what the heck is that?

1356
01:16:52,280 --> 01:16:56,280
So I would say five minutes later, it wasn't that long.

1357
01:16:56,280 --> 01:16:57,280
Ten minutes.

1358
01:16:57,280 --> 01:17:00,280
We see one of the helicopters from the Air Force base go out to it.

1359
01:17:00,280 --> 01:17:02,280
So they get up and they fly over it.

1360
01:17:02,280 --> 01:17:03,280
And they hover right over it.

1361
01:17:03,280 --> 01:17:04,280
It's still blinking.

1362
01:17:04,280 --> 01:17:05,280
It's not exploding.

1363
01:17:05,280 --> 01:17:06,280
It's still there.

1364
01:17:06,280 --> 01:17:07,280
Still blinking.

1365
01:17:07,280 --> 01:17:08,280
Just a nice pace.

1366
01:17:08,280 --> 01:17:10,280
Blink, blink, blink.

1367
01:17:10,280 --> 01:17:14,800
Helicopter hangs over, looks at it, doesn't do anything, goes all the way back.

1368
01:17:14,800 --> 01:17:17,560
So like, well, are they going to help the people?

1369
01:17:17,560 --> 01:17:20,560
Are they going to rescue them or are they going to do any of that?

1370
01:17:20,560 --> 01:17:21,560
Nothing.

1371
01:17:21,560 --> 01:17:22,850
That is so weird.

1372
01:17:22,850 --> 01:17:27,360
That's when it got fun.

1373
01:17:27,360 --> 01:17:32,360
So now, as we're watching this thing, it's about 10, 15, 20 minutes into it.

1374
01:17:32,360 --> 01:17:34,130
It gets closer.

1375
01:17:34,130 --> 01:17:35,420
It's still blinking.

1376
01:17:35,420 --> 01:17:36,420
It's still blinking.

1377
01:17:36,420 --> 01:17:37,420
It's getting closer.

1378
01:17:37,420 --> 01:17:38,420
It's leaving.

1379
01:17:38,420 --> 01:17:40,320
It's moving.

1380
01:17:40,320 --> 01:17:41,320
And then it gets within a mile.

1381
01:17:41,320 --> 01:17:42,320
So is that three miles?

1382
01:17:42,320 --> 01:17:43,320
Is that two miles?

1383
01:17:43,320 --> 01:17:46,480
It gets to about a half a mile.

1384
01:17:46,480 --> 01:17:50,480
And then somewhere at, I think, about a half a mile, it's not one light anymore.

1385
01:17:50,480 --> 01:17:53,370
It's split into six.

1386
01:17:53,370 --> 01:17:56,690
And it's not just getting bright.

1387
01:17:56,690 --> 01:18:01,690
These orange pinkish lights split and then they started rotating.

1388
01:18:01,690 --> 01:18:06,680
And they just started rotating like bicycle spokes on a wheel.

1389
01:18:06,680 --> 01:18:07,680
And they kept getting closer.

1390
01:18:07,680 --> 01:18:10,680
And they would go under the water and come back out, under the water, come back out,

1391
01:18:10,680 --> 01:18:12,680
under the water, come back out.

1392
01:18:12,680 --> 01:18:14,680
Like, this is really weird.

1393
01:18:14,680 --> 01:18:16,680
And they got closer to us.

1394
01:18:16,680 --> 01:18:20,680
So when it got about a quarter of a mile or maybe a thousand yards out, we're like, OK,

1395
01:18:20,680 --> 01:18:22,680
we're going to walk up the beach now.

1396
01:18:22,680 --> 01:18:23,680
That's been fun.

1397
01:18:23,680 --> 01:18:25,320
That's a little bit too close.

1398
01:18:25,320 --> 01:18:26,320
It kept following us.

1399
01:18:26,320 --> 01:18:27,320
It got closer.

1400
01:18:27,320 --> 01:18:28,320
It got closer.

1401
01:18:28,320 --> 01:18:29,320
It got brighter.

1402
01:18:29,320 --> 01:18:30,320
It got brighter.

1403
01:18:30,320 --> 01:18:37,000
And I think it was about when they got about, I wouldn't even be exaggerating if I said

1404
01:18:37,000 --> 01:18:38,000
50 yards.

1405
01:18:38,000 --> 01:18:39,000
We got that close.

1406
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:42,510
I started getting a little scared.

1407
01:18:42,510 --> 01:18:45,510
And I know she was getting scared.

1408
01:18:45,510 --> 01:18:50,510
Then, after about 40 minutes of looking at these lights and trying to run from them,

